# M7's "the release kernel contains no UART code", from the inside
# (user/root/src/release.rs; docs/design.md, "Scenarios" and "A release
# kernel without UART code"): the kernel built without features boots,
# prints nothing, and everything on COM1 after the loader comes from uart.
# xtask's disassembly check covers the kernel's code. The root task makes
# no debug system call; it issues COM1, IRQ 4 and, under QEMU,
# isa-debug-exit's 0xF4-0xF7, sets its exit port, starts watch, uart and
# console, attaches as client 1 and prints through console: its summary;
# that a probe thread's DebugPutChar, DebugHalt, DebugDumpScheduler and
# reserved numbers 19 and 31 each raised UnknownSyscall with the number in
# MR18 (root answers each with the probe's registers and ip + 2); the line
# the harness types, which reaches client 1 since focus starts there;
# uart's Stats; TEST PASS. Then a Sync, and IOPort_Out32(0xF4, 0x10) ends
# the run with success. The `next:` below puts root's first line right
# after the loader's last, so a kernel that printed anything at all fails;
# a kernel with debug would also print the lines forbidden below.
kernel: release
cmdline: test=release
exit: success
expect: loader: microL4 loader
expect: entering kernel
next: root: microL4 root task
expect: root: cmdline "test=release"
expect: root: image frames: slots
expect: root: empty: slots
expect: release: watch (priority 255), uart (priority 200) with the COM1 IOPort and IRQ 4, console (priority 150); exit port 0xf4-0xf7
expect: release: a probe thread's DebugPutChar, DebugHalt, DebugDumpScheduler and reserved numbers 19 and 31 each raised UnknownSyscall with the number in MR18
expect: release: type a line
send: release input\r
expect: release: read "release input"
expect: release: uart:
expect: , 14 bytes received,
expect: , 0 overruns, 0 line errors,
expect: TEST PASS
forbid: microL4 kernel
forbid: bootinfo:
forbid: DEBUG HALT
forbid: KERNEL PANIC
